[{:db/id 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-55b8ab85-3682-5003-bc82-d3e9f5248d03"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-55b8ab85-3682-5003-bc82-d3e9f5248d03" :question/id #uuid "55b8ab85-3682-5003-bc82-d3e9f5248d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-106755" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\n\nIII. $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although we have a product of an upper triangular matrix on the left and a unit lower triangular matrix on the right, the order of multiplication is not correct (instead, we need a unit lower triangular matrix on the left and an upper triangular matrix on the right).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5605219e-b32b-50d6-ae8e-13893dac1527"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5605219e-b32b-50d6-ae8e-13893dac1527" :answer-field/id #uuid "5605219e-b32b-50d6-ae8e-13893dac1527" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3907a7e-ba96-5506-8915-537e18e2116e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f3907a7e-ba96-5506-8915-537e18e2116e" "answer-f77569c8-f2a6-5605-a6af-f9b44459f38c" "answer-ad69335a-fa27-5de3-98db-67ed27d046b7" "answer-ecd4791a-30a0-5cef-b04a-83ca7b826af1" "answer-26a8adb1-6585-5d88-b2a9-a4c66146a7ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3907a7e-ba96-5506-8915-537e18e2116e" :answer/id #uuid "f3907a7e-ba96-5506-8915-537e18e2116e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f77569c8-f2a6-5605-a6af-f9b44459f38c" :answer/id #uuid "f77569c8-f2a6-5605-a6af-f9b44459f38c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad69335a-fa27-5de3-98db-67ed27d046b7" :answer/id #uuid "ad69335a-fa27-5de3-98db-67ed27d046b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecd4791a-30a0-5cef-b04a-83ca7b826af1" :answer/id #uuid "ecd4791a-30a0-5cef-b04a-83ca7b826af1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26a8adb1-6585-5d88-b2a9-a4c66146a7ef" :answer/id #uuid "26a8adb1-6585-5d88-b2a9-a4c66146a7ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-42d466fd-6c03-513d-b916-3193ae5d935b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-42d466fd-6c03-513d-b916-3193ae5d935b" :question/id #uuid "42d466fd-6c03-513d-b916-3193ae5d935b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106766" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 9\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-7){R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=7,{u}_{22}=-5,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{12}=-35.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e192a93-84a5-59c0-884b-235a349cd678"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e192a93-84a5-59c0-884b-235a349cd678" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e192a93-84a5-59c0-884b-235a349cd678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bc2c0f77-5481-5f8a-b556-ff5507543ca5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc2c0f77-5481-5f8a-b556-ff5507543ca5" "answer-76a16c2d-6a05-575e-a83a-271e0b390c85" "answer-726c8472-17c5-5d1f-9c91-e04c085b468c" "answer-dfb28c55-d1c7-5022-adb7-21280b2bfcb7" "answer-8bed455b-9692-567b-9f57-f93f82c4503d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc2c0f77-5481-5f8a-b556-ff5507543ca5" :answer/id #uuid "bc2c0f77-5481-5f8a-b556-ff5507543ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76a16c2d-6a05-575e-a83a-271e0b390c85" :answer/id #uuid "76a16c2d-6a05-575e-a83a-271e0b390c85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-726c8472-17c5-5d1f-9c91-e04c085b468c" :answer/id #uuid "726c8472-17c5-5d1f-9c91-e04c085b468c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfb28c55-d1c7-5022-adb7-21280b2bfcb7" :answer/id #uuid "dfb28c55-d1c7-5022-adb7-21280b2bfcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bed455b-9692-567b-9f57-f93f82c4503d" :answer/id #uuid "8bed455b-9692-567b-9f57-f93f82c4503d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119793 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d20ab7a7-2299-5eca-8c7e-9709ddaf034c" "question-1cf3361e-986e-5750-bf9f-73762dff3b0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d20ab7a7-2299-5eca-8c7e-9709ddaf034c" :question/id #uuid "d20ab7a7-2299-5eca-8c7e-9709ddaf034c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32547" :question/problem "Given that\n $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -9\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-3,{u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bb19108-7f19-5591-ae3c-6544894088fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bb19108-7f19-5591-ae3c-6544894088fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb19108-7f19-5591-ae3c-6544894088fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49cdf79c-58f3-5591-94f0-0d48ea2d4f6c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49cdf79c-58f3-5591-94f0-0d48ea2d4f6c" "answer-4da3e47c-22f5-5965-908e-6f3b266993d1" "answer-2d7c47e5-bc18-5759-9dba-bef203ec6a76" "answer-c847da6e-0099-5446-9b32-bda4703a56ba" "answer-382d6998-098c-5ac8-a4eb-2cf87144df8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49cdf79c-58f3-5591-94f0-0d48ea2d4f6c" :answer/id #uuid "49cdf79c-58f3-5591-94f0-0d48ea2d4f6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4da3e47c-22f5-5965-908e-6f3b266993d1" :answer/id #uuid "4da3e47c-22f5-5965-908e-6f3b266993d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d7c47e5-bc18-5759-9dba-bef203ec6a76" :answer/id #uuid "2d7c47e5-bc18-5759-9dba-bef203ec6a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c847da6e-0099-5446-9b32-bda4703a56ba" :answer/id #uuid "c847da6e-0099-5446-9b32-bda4703a56ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-382d6998-098c-5ac8-a4eb-2cf87144df8e" :answer/id #uuid "382d6998-098c-5ac8-a4eb-2cf87144df8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1cf3361e-986e-5750-bf9f-73762dff3b0e" :question/id #uuid "1cf3361e-986e-5750-bf9f-73762dff3b0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106771" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=\\frac{1}{2},$ ${u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-89806148-2b04-5dff-9c9d-9aecabad8125"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89806148-2b04-5dff-9c9d-9aecabad8125" :answer-field/id #uuid "89806148-2b04-5dff-9c9d-9aecabad8125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ac5ab758-9dd9-5005-99ab-90aa7d7d9c95" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d113435-7d4d-5e64-bf7a-6096265af4ef" "answer-97a99f95-7b5c-511f-b1dd-63628675fb7e" "answer-b15e8623-fcd9-53a6-8695-28d9aee82949" "answer-ac5ab758-9dd9-5005-99ab-90aa7d7d9c95" "answer-25d6bf9d-c36b-57f4-a4a3-d6d10d20a9fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d113435-7d4d-5e64-bf7a-6096265af4ef" :answer/id #uuid "2d113435-7d4d-5e64-bf7a-6096265af4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97a99f95-7b5c-511f-b1dd-63628675fb7e" :answer/id #uuid "97a99f95-7b5c-511f-b1dd-63628675fb7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b15e8623-fcd9-53a6-8695-28d9aee82949" :answer/id #uuid "b15e8623-fcd9-53a6-8695-28d9aee82949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac5ab758-9dd9-5005-99ab-90aa7d7d9c95" :answer/id #uuid "ac5ab758-9dd9-5005-99ab-90aa7d7d9c95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d6bf9d-c36b-57f4-a4a3-d6d10d20a9fe" :answer/id #uuid "25d6bf9d-c36b-57f4-a4a3-d6d10d20a9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121028 :tutorial/content "In the same way that we can factor numbers or polynomials, we can factor a matrix by writing it as a product of two or more matrices. In fact, there is one factorization technique that works for *all* matrices, called **LU factorization** (or **LU decomposition**).\n\nLU factorization involves writing a matrix $A$ as a product of two matrices $L$ and $U,$ where\n\n- ![](images/ad/adca162da15cab5989e5726acb495fc12533231c2e38b0392d68388aeb18493b.svg) is a *unit lower triangular matrix* (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal), and\n\n- ![](images/93/93338df4d1ee1791dc5b1679dbddff34d94d05677c362b1a41dcb925ca83a1dc.svg) is an *upper triangular matrix*.\n\nFor example, we can write the matrix ![](images/83/835b8ad372998cbb35be4c1998d236fe96f1d1b03ee1ad7062bdbbb77e254bf6.svg) in LU factored form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nYou may be wondering how we arrived at this factorization. Shortly, we'll discuss an algorithm that explains how to compute $L$ and $U$ for any $2\\times2$ matrix $A.$ But for now, let's focus on recognizing LU factored forms." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121067 :tutorial/content "Let ![](images/ff/ff7b3f4bca1676cbe3fb78ae1c2a47d8fd0bc71dd98dee4c7b6fea4cc94ec7bd.svg) To perform LU factorization, we need to write $A$ as \n\n![](images/3f/3f74fdde04340f6a4dbd86962f5a31f8af22b5fb8053c66fa3e8be41629b12a1.svg)\n\nTo find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since $E_1A=U,$ we can invert $E_1$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Caution:** To get a unit lower triangular matrix at the end, we have the following restriction while reducing a matrix $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n- we can only add a multiple of the $1$st row to the $2$nd row ($R_2:=R_2+k R_1$), and\n\n- the other elementary row operations (swapping or multiplying a row by a number) are not allowed." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096762 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9b1a0e36-dce4-509e-90b0-4f68fe84ad7d" "question-b28f59d7-76e7-504d-aaab-0c27b75b3222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b1a0e36-dce4-509e-90b0-4f68fe84ad7d" :question/id #uuid "9b1a0e36-dce4-509e-90b0-4f68fe84ad7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84968" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x+5)^{2}=-3(y-6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{4})(y-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=-5$ and $k=6.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(-5,6).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eada811c-d053-5120-a961-fe8ffd045312"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eada811c-d053-5120-a961-fe8ffd045312" :answer-field/id #uuid "eada811c-d053-5120-a961-fe8ffd045312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6de35bfe-a94a-5f6f-a2a7-be882652597a" "answer-1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" "answer-f833dfc3-dd27-5cc6-a187-eb5f1348d40e" "answer-6332f8e1-70e3-52dc-ba10-2ad158c200d7" "answer-98125233-946f-554a-8efb-6031235b27b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6de35bfe-a94a-5f6f-a2a7-be882652597a" :answer/id #uuid "6de35bfe-a94a-5f6f-a2a7-be882652597a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" :answer/id #uuid "1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f833dfc3-dd27-5cc6-a187-eb5f1348d40e" :answer/id #uuid "f833dfc3-dd27-5cc6-a187-eb5f1348d40e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6332f8e1-70e3-52dc-ba10-2ad158c200d7" :answer/id #uuid "6332f8e1-70e3-52dc-ba10-2ad158c200d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98125233-946f-554a-8efb-6031235b27b4" :answer/id #uuid "98125233-946f-554a-8efb-6031235b27b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(6,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096763 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-206046fc-72eb-5e7e-8330-c7dfc01fc134" "question-9b2b25e3-0202-54b4-aedb-ceb8981dd37f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-206046fc-72eb-5e7e-8330-c7dfc01fc134" :question/id #uuid "206046fc-72eb-5e7e-8330-c7dfc01fc134" :question/math-academy-id "q-84976" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-2(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y-0)^{2}=4(-\\frac{2}{4})(x-1),\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n(y-0)^{2}=4(-\\frac{1}{2})(x-1).\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=1$ and $k=0.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8abcfe54-e8c7-5c1d-9465-cff1e4813088"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8abcfe54-e8c7-5c1d-9465-cff1e4813088" :answer-field/id #uuid "8abcfe54-e8c7-5c1d-9465-cff1e4813088" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2718af2e-0e58-5f94-b179-4b6122d8bbc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20e4a15a-eda1-52a1-8baa-9cdce6bed32e" "answer-84737793-7f74-5db9-b6ff-72f64548ee3c" "answer-e5f0f01f-aa87-552e-8444-03f833352b21" "answer-2718af2e-0e58-5f94-b179-4b6122d8bbc8" "answer-959f0371-d54d-54ee-88dc-a7c52e86bcd9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20e4a15a-eda1-52a1-8baa-9cdce6bed32e" :answer/id #uuid "20e4a15a-eda1-52a1-8baa-9cdce6bed32e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84737793-7f74-5db9-b6ff-72f64548ee3c" :answer/id #uuid "84737793-7f74-5db9-b6ff-72f64548ee3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5f0f01f-aa87-552e-8444-03f833352b21" :answer/id #uuid "e5f0f01f-aa87-552e-8444-03f833352b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2718af2e-0e58-5f94-b179-4b6122d8bbc8" :answer/id #uuid "2718af2e-0e58-5f94-b179-4b6122d8bbc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-959f0371-d54d-54ee-88dc-a7c52e86bcd9" :answer/id #uuid "959f0371-d54d-54ee-88dc-a7c52e86bcd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b28f59d7-76e7-504d-aaab-0c27b75b3222" :question/id #uuid "b28f59d7-76e7-504d-aaab-0c27b75b3222" :question/math-academy-id "q-115904" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x-4)^{2}=-24(y+5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4(-6)(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-6.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=4$ and $k=-5.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(4,-5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d580fbee-d419-5754-8c6e-c8cdde3856be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d580fbee-d419-5754-8c6e-c8cdde3856be" :answer-field/id #uuid "d580fbee-d419-5754-8c6e-c8cdde3856be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81efdfb9-02a6-5ea4-a9eb-5456a31d6ea3" "answer-11ba3512-eaa8-5321-aa96-abe2a946d071" "answer-d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" "answer-95dd750a-51eb-54bf-b675-b53b71df0478" "answer-8406d667-63ff-58a4-a718-2dd90e66256a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81efdfb9-02a6-5ea4-a9eb-5456a31d6ea3" :answer/id #uuid "81efdfb9-02a6-5ea4-a9eb-5456a31d6ea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11ba3512-eaa8-5321-aa96-abe2a946d071" :answer/id #uuid "11ba3512-eaa8-5321-aa96-abe2a946d071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-6,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" :answer/id #uuid "d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95dd750a-51eb-54bf-b675-b53b71df0478" :answer/id #uuid "95dd750a-51eb-54bf-b675-b53b71df0478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8406d667-63ff-58a4-a718-2dd90e66256a" :answer/id #uuid "8406d667-63ff-58a4-a718-2dd90e66256a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b2b25e3-0202-54b4-aedb-ceb8981dd37f" :question/id #uuid "9b2b25e3-0202-54b4-aedb-ceb8981dd37f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115907" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=16x?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(4)x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=4.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38d93762-7c0b-561a-b5d6-707d86a75a3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38d93762-7c0b-561a-b5d6-707d86a75a3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "38d93762-7c0b-561a-b5d6-707d86a75a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a02ee2b-c276-5b3b-b415-d7b395c5780c" "answer-90e56bb0-d61e-5cde-bde8-277de6795d05" "answer-87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" "answer-6e170e66-986b-586b-aa37-931b2ef7939d" "answer-f5c30631-442c-5970-930d-6fbc7ef97378"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a02ee2b-c276-5b3b-b415-d7b395c5780c" :answer/id #uuid "8a02ee2b-c276-5b3b-b415-d7b395c5780c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90e56bb0-d61e-5cde-bde8-277de6795d05" :answer/id #uuid "90e56bb0-d61e-5cde-bde8-277de6795d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-16)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" :answer/id #uuid "87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e170e66-986b-586b-aa37-931b2ef7939d" :answer/id #uuid "6e170e66-986b-586b-aa37-931b2ef7939d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5c30631-442c-5970-930d-6fbc7ef97378" :answer/id #uuid "f5c30631-442c-5970-930d-6fbc7ef97378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(16,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0cad29d4-752e-5cc0-8c92-569e4d3b7028" :activity/id #uuid "0cad29d4-752e-5cc0-8c92-569e4d3b7028" :activity/title "The Vertex of a Parabola" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049336 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3ea97b63-e85c-5154-a3c9-5557381da863" "step-c7de61d8-86cc-5e37-ae5a-5f91aacc8f90" "step-1de71a91-5927-5d94-a614-8888a06224ab" "step-0e9037ca-ed1b-570a-8dcc-c8bad6548089" "step-c004f194-0740-5260-a541-251ce197b566"] :activity/first-step "step-3ea97b63-e85c-5154-a3c9-5557381da863" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3ea97b63-e85c-5154-a3c9-5557381da863" :step/id #uuid "3ea97b63-e85c-5154-a3c9-5557381da863" :step/content "question-9b1a0e36-dce4-509e-90b0-4f68fe84ad7d" :step/next "step-c7de61d8-86cc-5e37-ae5a-5f91aacc8f90" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c7de61d8-86cc-5e37-ae5a-5f91aacc8f90" :step/id #uuid "c7de61d8-86cc-5e37-ae5a-5f91aacc8f90" :step/content "question-206046fc-72eb-5e7e-8330-c7dfc01fc134" :step/next "step-1de71a91-5927-5d94-a614-8888a06224ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1de71a91-5927-5d94-a614-8888a06224ab" :step/id #uuid "1de71a91-5927-5d94-a614-8888a06224ab" :step/content 17592186250503 :step/next "step-0e9037ca-ed1b-570a-8dcc-c8bad6548089" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0e9037ca-ed1b-570a-8dcc-c8bad6548089" :step/id #uuid "0e9037ca-ed1b-570a-8dcc-c8bad6548089" :step/content "question-b28f59d7-76e7-504d-aaab-0c27b75b3222" :step/next "step-c004f194-0740-5260-a541-251ce197b566" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c004f194-0740-5260-a541-251ce197b566" :step/id #uuid "c004f194-0740-5260-a541-251ce197b566" :step/content "question-9b2b25e3-0202-54b4-aedb-ceb8981dd37f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186109459 :answer-field/choices 17592186109460] [:db/retract 17592186109459 :answer-field/choices 17592186109461] [:db/retract 17592186109459 :answer-field/choices 17592186109462] [:db/retract 17592186109459 :answer-field/choices 17592186109463] [:db/retract 17592186109459 :answer-field/choices 17592186109464] [:db/retract 17592186109477 :answer-field/choices 17592186109478] [:db/retract 17592186109477 :answer-field/choices 17592186109479] [:db/retract 17592186109477 :answer-field/choices 17592186109480] [:db/retract 17592186109477 :answer-field/choices 17592186109481] [:db/retract 17592186109477 :answer-field/choices 17592186109482] {:db/id 17592186111289 :question/problem "![](images/27/2772e28367d49fcf0e2503b7cdd5d5aae5ea217b7060b288f9fb6e149ee25f57.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the rectangle $LMNP$ above equals $22\\,cm.$ What is the length of $\\overset{―}{NP}?$" :question/worked-solution "The opposite sides of a rectangle are congruent, so we have\n\n$$\nPL=MN=3\\,cm.\n$$\n\nFor the same reason, we also have\n\n$$\nNP=LM.\n$$\n\nNow, since the perimeter is $p=22\\,\\text{cm},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =LM+MN+NP+PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+2PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+6 \\\\ 16 & =2NP \\\\ 8 & =NP\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $NP=8\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109459 :answer-field/correct "answer-8ef276f9-82e0-540a-a7aa-3df3cd37ef1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45862696-e078-5e44-908a-932757756e30" "answer-819ae118-95dd-5f4e-9632-632e6a720f7e" "answer-8fefaa4b-1f74-555a-813d-ef2559bd86ef" "answer-8ef276f9-82e0-540a-a7aa-3df3cd37ef1d" "answer-e06896fa-1962-56fe-8a72-6a43c2652c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45862696-e078-5e44-908a-932757756e30" :answer/id #uuid "45862696-e078-5e44-908a-932757756e30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-819ae118-95dd-5f4e-9632-632e6a720f7e" :answer/id #uuid "819ae118-95dd-5f4e-9632-632e6a720f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fefaa4b-1f74-555a-813d-ef2559bd86ef" :answer/id #uuid "8fefaa4b-1f74-555a-813d-ef2559bd86ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ef276f9-82e0-540a-a7aa-3df3cd37ef1d" :answer/id #uuid "8ef276f9-82e0-540a-a7aa-3df3cd37ef1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e06896fa-1962-56fe-8a72-6a43c2652c9c" :answer/id #uuid "e06896fa-1962-56fe-8a72-6a43c2652c9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,cm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110783 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7693917f-3fc9-5b3a-9850-3e604834da65"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111291 :question/worked-solution "If $PQRS$ is a square, then $m∠QSP={45}^{∘}.$ Now,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QSP & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ (2t+7)^{∘} & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ 2t & =38 \\\\ t & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109471 :answer-field/correct 17592186109475 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110782 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a8ecca8c-4ba9-51a9-9a23-0b141e2831c4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111292 :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b2ade26c577b7362460f55397024e3b321a54d769fe1c412f79f38b17f40806.png)\n\nIn a square above, $PO=5\\,mm.$ Find $QS.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonals of a square are equal and bisect each other. So we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QS & =PR \\\\  & =2PO \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5\\,mm \\\\  & =10\\,mm.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109477 :answer-field/correct "answer-86375367-a91a-58af-b9b9-c25b2769c970" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86375367-a91a-58af-b9b9-c25b2769c970" "answer-fb5ccb6f-35e3-5aaa-9b9d-aa15fc253253" "answer-a612b194-ad13-5f18-8c42-e680666dd5f5" "answer-ab0051b0-2deb-5281-b8f1-683298088071" "answer-8e69bf76-adcd-5423-bdf5-ebc4e9bca2fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86375367-a91a-58af-b9b9-c25b2769c970" :answer/id #uuid "86375367-a91a-58af-b9b9-c25b2769c970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,mm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb5ccb6f-35e3-5aaa-9b9d-aa15fc253253" :answer/id #uuid "fb5ccb6f-35e3-5aaa-9b9d-aa15fc253253" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,mm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a612b194-ad13-5f18-8c42-e680666dd5f5" :answer/id #uuid "a612b194-ad13-5f18-8c42-e680666dd5f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,mm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab0051b0-2deb-5281-b8f1-683298088071" :answer/id #uuid "ab0051b0-2deb-5281-b8f1-683298088071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,mm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e69bf76-adcd-5423-bdf5-ebc4e9bca2fc" :answer/id #uuid "8e69bf76-adcd-5423-bdf5-ebc4e9bca2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,mm" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8ecca8c-4ba9-51a9-9a23-0b141e2831c4" :question/id #uuid "a8ecca8c-4ba9-51a9-9a23-0b141e2831c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-129308" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c897e2e9b209470f24964b5c00d4e79e4f056a2cbcab4e1e1a1651e949291537.png)\n\nIn a square above, $PO=2.5\\,m.$ Find $QS.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonals of a square are equal and bisect each other. So we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QS & =PR \\\\  & =2PO \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2.5\\,m \\\\  & =5\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5786cd11-3148-5ae6-b45b-9cd70b618e71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5786cd11-3148-5ae6-b45b-9cd70b618e71" :answer-field/id #uuid "5786cd11-3148-5ae6-b45b-9cd70b618e71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fafaa12b-38a2-5687-86e2-c0e87e67bbb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3dddf3d-1092-572e-9d02-c926c7039d94" "answer-fafaa12b-38a2-5687-86e2-c0e87e67bbb1" "answer-2cd64979-6e41-5feb-9763-12b70161a8db" "answer-768762c7-e409-5b41-8927-e05be0bd5283" "answer-73e7f063-2389-5ce2-b5d8-4354922bf5d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3dddf3d-1092-572e-9d02-c926c7039d94" :answer/id #uuid "d3dddf3d-1092-572e-9d02-c926c7039d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fafaa12b-38a2-5687-86e2-c0e87e67bbb1" :answer/id #uuid "fafaa12b-38a2-5687-86e2-c0e87e67bbb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cd64979-6e41-5feb-9763-12b70161a8db" :answer/id #uuid "2cd64979-6e41-5feb-9763-12b70161a8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-768762c7-e409-5b41-8927-e05be0bd5283" :answer/id #uuid "768762c7-e409-5b41-8927-e05be0bd5283" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73e7f063-2389-5ce2-b5d8-4354922bf5d6" :answer/id #uuid "73e7f063-2389-5ce2-b5d8-4354922bf5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7693917f-3fc9-5b3a-9850-3e604834da65" :question/id #uuid "7693917f-3fc9-5b3a-9850-3e604834da65" :question/math-academy-id "q-129313" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b68ede517afc0d8fd6ce6a110ed261a805a3218d6afee3caaed88c73d6e3763e.png)\n\nFor which value of $t$ is the rectangle above also a square?" :question/worked-solution "If $PQRS$ is a square, then $m∠RSQ={45}^{∘}.$ Now,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RSQ & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ (6t+3)^{∘} & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ 6t & =42 \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2fe3cb9b-6905-5041-9d17-a4bc0c8f8821"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2fe3cb9b-6905-5041-9d17-a4bc0c8f8821" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe3cb9b-6905-5041-9d17-a4bc0c8f8821" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d9659e3b-cc3b-57e6-9d57-cf48990885e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d248db1-d0cc-5479-b350-a7ff11f897d5" "answer-4a0dcc81-1ecd-57bc-9357-ff2f778c95e7" "answer-d9659e3b-cc3b-57e6-9d57-cf48990885e4" "answer-46724bfe-a2b9-5992-bb9e-b42ddd06cc26" "answer-64df6060-c12a-5501-9bc1-f7cebcffdda2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d248db1-d0cc-5479-b350-a7ff11f897d5" :answer/id #uuid "4d248db1-d0cc-5479-b350-a7ff11f897d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a0dcc81-1ecd-57bc-9357-ff2f778c95e7" :answer/id #uuid "4a0dcc81-1ecd-57bc-9357-ff2f778c95e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9659e3b-cc3b-57e6-9d57-cf48990885e4" :answer/id #uuid "d9659e3b-cc3b-57e6-9d57-cf48990885e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46724bfe-a2b9-5992-bb9e-b42ddd06cc26" :answer/id #uuid "46724bfe-a2b9-5992-bb9e-b42ddd06cc26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64df6060-c12a-5501-9bc1-f7cebcffdda2" :answer/id #uuid "64df6060-c12a-5501-9bc1-f7cebcffdda2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0f43d605-4de8-5ca6-b506-35d97f68e93e" :activity/id #uuid "0f43d605-4de8-5ca6-b506-35d97f68e93e" :activity/title "Properties of Rectangles and Squares" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048360 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-905ca13b-6f9e-5145-a548-eaaad57e2c4d" "step-cab314ab-243b-514f-8462-43e2920a2fbb" "step-1027e455-5ee4-575f-a6cc-57b6e880e238" "step-331bf58f-c42b-59b1-905e-d63cfda6b8f6" "step-b1723b82-78c4-51dd-bd56-4ef24607eb2d"] :activity/first-step "step-905ca13b-6f9e-5145-a548-eaaad57e2c4d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-905ca13b-6f9e-5145-a548-eaaad57e2c4d" :step/id #uuid "905ca13b-6f9e-5145-a548-eaaad57e2c4d" :step/content 17592186111289 :step/next "step-cab314ab-243b-514f-8462-43e2920a2fbb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cab314ab-243b-514f-8462-43e2920a2fbb" :step/id #uuid "cab314ab-243b-514f-8462-43e2920a2fbb" :step/content 17592186111291 :step/next "step-1027e455-5ee4-575f-a6cc-57b6e880e238" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1027e455-5ee4-575f-a6cc-57b6e880e238" :step/id #uuid "1027e455-5ee4-575f-a6cc-57b6e880e238" :step/content 17592186111292 :step/next "step-331bf58f-c42b-59b1-905e-d63cfda6b8f6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-331bf58f-c42b-59b1-905e-d63cfda6b8f6" :step/id #uuid "331bf58f-c42b-59b1-905e-d63cfda6b8f6" :step/content "question-a8ecca8c-4ba9-51a9-9a23-0b141e2831c4" :step/next "step-b1723b82-78c4-51dd-bd56-4ef24607eb2d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b1723b82-78c4-51dd-bd56-4ef24607eb2d" :step/id #uuid "b1723b82-78c4-51dd-bd56-4ef24607eb2d" :step/content "question-7693917f-3fc9-5b3a-9850-3e604834da65" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33b0ba11-b389-5606-bdc5-3231dc03a907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33b0ba11-b389-5606-bdc5-3231dc03a907" :question/id #uuid "33b0ba11-b389-5606-bdc5-3231dc03a907" :question/math-academy-id "q-54628" :question/problem "If $6{q}^{2}+2=0$, then $q=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{q}^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ 6{q}^{2} & =-2 \\\\ {q}^{2} & =-\\frac{2}{6} \\\\ {q}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nq=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $q$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85af8f72-ec85-54b7-a8f7-5877f671a615"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85af8f72-ec85-54b7-a8f7-5877f671a615" :answer-field/id #uuid "85af8f72-ec85-54b7-a8f7-5877f671a615" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4b7d13a5-cae4-55c5-8414-98b27b21b2fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37230d2e-ba17-5538-a122-3990a8fad384" "answer-4b7d13a5-cae4-55c5-8414-98b27b21b2fc" "answer-afeb9c99-445c-517d-ae58-6bc31a2f160d" "answer-a1d7dc8a-bfe3-53e5-b5c5-922f209d8203" "answer-a85abb46-eab6-5a77-981e-c5102ce9118d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37230d2e-ba17-5538-a122-3990a8fad384" :answer/id #uuid "37230d2e-ba17-5538-a122-3990a8fad384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b7d13a5-cae4-55c5-8414-98b27b21b2fc" :answer/id #uuid "4b7d13a5-cae4-55c5-8414-98b27b21b2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afeb9c99-445c-517d-ae58-6bc31a2f160d" :answer/id #uuid "afeb9c99-445c-517d-ae58-6bc31a2f160d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d7dc8a-bfe3-53e5-b5c5-922f209d8203" :answer/id #uuid "a1d7dc8a-bfe3-53e5-b5c5-922f209d8203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a85abb46-eab6-5a77-981e-c5102ce9118d" :answer/id #uuid "a85abb46-eab6-5a77-981e-c5102ce9118d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-45c755e7-98dd-5776-8bcf-226024a31c7b" "question-2ac537c1-52d1-57f6-aadf-0ba9eddf7efc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-45c755e7-98dd-5776-8bcf-226024a31c7b" :question/id #uuid "45c755e7-98dd-5776-8bcf-226024a31c7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-66253" :question/problem "Find the solutions of the equation $16{y}^{2}+4=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 16{y}^{2} & =-4 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{16} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{4}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef84a2ef-fc28-5057-b639-100cb5c08721"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef84a2ef-fc28-5057-b639-100cb5c08721" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef84a2ef-fc28-5057-b639-100cb5c08721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd4c32b3-b5a3-5c89-bd62-97a30efe2dab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-908fc347-0be1-50c0-99cd-da5164897e6a" "answer-dd4c32b3-b5a3-5c89-bd62-97a30efe2dab" "answer-d76312f5-0e57-5076-954e-87ce4299933b" "answer-4d75c601-096a-5903-b04a-0034749e71d5" "answer-982355ec-96f1-512b-a246-51b13af7a290"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-908fc347-0be1-50c0-99cd-da5164897e6a" :answer/id #uuid "908fc347-0be1-50c0-99cd-da5164897e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd4c32b3-b5a3-5c89-bd62-97a30efe2dab" :answer/id #uuid "dd4c32b3-b5a3-5c89-bd62-97a30efe2dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d76312f5-0e57-5076-954e-87ce4299933b" :answer/id #uuid "d76312f5-0e57-5076-954e-87ce4299933b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d75c601-096a-5903-b04a-0034749e71d5" :answer/id #uuid "4d75c601-096a-5903-b04a-0034749e71d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-982355ec-96f1-512b-a246-51b13af7a290" :answer/id #uuid "982355ec-96f1-512b-a246-51b13af7a290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ac537c1-52d1-57f6-aadf-0ba9eddf7efc" :question/id #uuid "2ac537c1-52d1-57f6-aadf-0ba9eddf7efc" :question/math-academy-id "q-66255" :question/problem "Find the solutions of the equation $25{p}^{2}+9=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{p}^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ 25{p}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ {p}^{2} & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\np=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{25}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf2cb22a-fba8-530e-bbc8-7944b15ca76e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf2cb22a-fba8-530e-bbc8-7944b15ca76e" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf2cb22a-fba8-530e-bbc8-7944b15ca76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c1a101c1-9786-5d88-9209-fcc7d448aa1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb0d414b-e1c0-5c88-ab3f-bff76e81cf3d" "answer-99e9c2d9-ca71-5f4e-b523-91dfc1e79109" "answer-dc5e6b1f-04e3-59e8-87a8-e323755f3073" "answer-c1a101c1-9786-5d88-9209-fcc7d448aa1f" "answer-948c20ce-c92b-55b2-b01e-52c62ba0d702"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb0d414b-e1c0-5c88-ab3f-bff76e81cf3d" :answer/id #uuid "eb0d414b-e1c0-5c88-ab3f-bff76e81cf3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99e9c2d9-ca71-5f4e-b523-91dfc1e79109" :answer/id #uuid "99e9c2d9-ca71-5f4e-b523-91dfc1e79109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc5e6b1f-04e3-59e8-87a8-e323755f3073" :answer/id #uuid "dc5e6b1f-04e3-59e8-87a8-e323755f3073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1a101c1-9786-5d88-9209-fcc7d448aa1f" :answer/id #uuid "c1a101c1-9786-5d88-9209-fcc7d448aa1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-948c20ce-c92b-55b2-b01