\\\ -xy+4x & =2y-5 \\\\ 4x+5 & =xy+2y \\\\ 4x+5 & =y(x+2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0c890417-6b3f-5bb6-b26f-482f2ab4cfca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0c890417-6b3f-5bb6-b26f-482f2ab4cfca" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c890417-6b3f-5bb6-b26f-482f2ab4cfca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57" :answer/id #uuid "d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-411f5065-9d51-51d9-906e-20eb90eb5d15" :question/id #uuid "411f5065-9d51-51d9-906e-20eb90eb5d15" :question/math-academy-id "q-148507" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x & =\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x(5y+1) & =y-8 \\\\ -5xy-x & =y-8 \\\\ 8-x & =5xy+y \\\\ 8-x & =y(5x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8d60ccb-7323-5847-8254-46df29873deb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8d60ccb-7323-5847-8254-46df29873deb" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d60ccb-7323-5847-8254-46df29873deb" :answer-field/key "selec