ned}x & =\\frac{2y-1}{y+3} \\\\ x(y+3) & =2y-1 \\\\ xy+3x & =2y-1 \\\\ 3x+1 & =2y-xy \\\\ 3x+1 & =y(2-x) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x+1}{2-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+1}{2-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ac282e1-a856-594b-be2b-702b41e1fdc2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ac282e1-a856-594b-be2b-702b41e1fdc2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac282e1-a856-594b-be2b-702b41e1fdc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e39ef11-c972-593e-a0d4-7e6de8c0916d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fd02d5c-098e-5bda-aef9-22dfd59c8033" "answer-9f0b91ef-dfcc-59c1-86ef-6696e2a00f41" "answer-6699e128-718f-5db1-8a5f-945b88bd793a" "answer-7e39ef11-c972-593e-a0d4-7e6de8c0916d" "answer-e17b707f-0130-5fa7-b360-4dcc6e6ed3e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fd02d5c-098e-5bda-aef9-22dfd59c8033" :answer/id #uuid "6fd02d5c-098e-5bda-aef9-22dfd59c8033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-2x}{x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f0b91ef-dfcc-59c1-86ef-6696e2a00f41" :answer/id #uuid "9f0b91ef-dfcc-59c1-86ef-6696e2a00f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-3x}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6699e128-718f-5db1-8a5f-945b88bd793a" :answer/id #uuid "6699e128-718f-5db1-8a5f-945b88bd793a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-3x}{x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e39ef11-c972-593e-a0d4-7e6de8c0916d" :answer/id #uuid "7e39ef11-c972-593e-a0d4-7e6de8c0916d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+1}{2-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e17b707f-0130-5fa7-b360-4dcc6e6ed3e0" :answer/id #uuid "e17b707f-0130-5fa7-b360-4dcc6e6ed3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+3}{x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-de7ae964-9fce-58b0-bd1b-ba5303123396" :question/id #uuid "de7ae964-9fce-58b0-bd1b-ba5303123396" :question/math-academy-id "q-148508" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5-2y}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5-2y}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =5-2y \\\\ xy+x & =5-2y \\\\ xy+2y & =5-x \\\\ y(x+2) & =5-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5-x}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59384b78-3cc9-5dfa-a137-2e35558b2a9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59384b78-3cc9-5dfa-a137-2e35558b2a9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "59384b78-3cc9-5dfa-a137-2e35558b2a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20e7484f-fbbe-5b08-bcac-c2785c1893e9" "answer-968e8cbc-ee3b-507c-836c-108dd308cb48" "answer-016428bb-9b2a-5acd-8baf-3acf6f1ba744" "answer-ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" "answer-9f87e1ab-5c04-53d3-9116-9fa836141840"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20e7484f-fbbe-5b08-bcac-c2785c1893e9" :answer/id #uuid "20e7484f-fbbe-5b08-bcac-c2785c1893e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{2x-5}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-968e8cbc-ee3b-507c-836c-108dd308cb48" :answer/id #uuid "968e8cbc-ee3b-507c-836c-108dd308cb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-016428bb-9b2a-5acd-8baf-3acf6f1ba744" :answer/id #uuid "016428bb-9b2a-5acd-8baf-3acf6f1ba744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" :answer/id #uuid "ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f87e1ab-5c04-53d3-9116-9fa836141840" :answer/id #uuid "9f87e1ab-5c04-53d3-9116-9fa836141840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+5}{2-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-754f4c4b-11dc-5f96-9fa9-3c28fe7e8a39" :question/id #uuid "754f4c4b-11dc-5f96-9fa9-3c28fe7e8a39" :question/math-academy-id "q-148584" :question/problem "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1},\\,x\\ne 1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-8}{x-2},\\,x\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2y+k}{y-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2y+k}{y-1} \\\\ x(y-1) & =2y+k \\\\ xy-x & =2y+k \\\\ xy-2y & =x+k \\\\ y(x-2) & =x+k \\\\ y & =\\frac{x+k}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+k}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16bcada1-2264-5573-b603-5074361a0f9f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16bcada1-2264-5573-b603-5074361a0f9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "16bcada1-2264-5573-b603-5074361a0f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0827d445-54bb-5a4c-8341-aefe90394569" "answer-b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" "answer-5f2e54fc-a95a-5356-b970-579dea53d954" "answer-f5842b48-e760-5215-af2b-61005182e37e" "answer-b2c4dd6b-e1c5-52bc-9780-636b2e616133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0827d445-54bb-5a4c-8341-aefe90394569" :answer/id #uuid "0827d445-54bb-5a4c-8341-aefe90394569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" :answer/id #uuid "b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f2e54fc-a95a-5356-b970-579dea53d954" :answer/id #uuid "5f2e54fc-a95a-5356-b970-579dea53d954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5842b48-e760-5215-af2b-61005182e37e" :answer/id #uuid "f5842b48-e760-5215-af2b-61005182e37e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2c4dd6b-e1c5-52bc-9780-636b2e616133" :answer/id #uuid "b2c4dd6b-e1c5-52bc-9780-636b2e616133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e33bcefe-71b8-5e01-9202-e30bde07e783" :question/id #uuid "e33bcefe-71b8-5e01-9202-e30bde07e783" :question/math-academy-id "q-276781" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9-6x}{4x}.$ What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3k}{6+4y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x(6+4y) & =3k \\\\ 6x+4xy & =3k \\\\ 4xy & =3k-6x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2b18f9b-8d04-502e-a1b1-ced120e8f787"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2b18f9b-8d04-502e-a1b1-ced120e8f787" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b18f9b-8d04-502e-a1b1-ced120e8f787" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92" :answer/id #uuid "b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa405f43-aa49-5df2-9659-18d1b520e384" :question/id #uuid "fa405f43-aa49-5df2-9659-18d1b520e384" :question/math-academy-id "q-148537" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{7x+k}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1+3x}{7x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{7x+k}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{7y+k}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{7y+k} \\\\ x(7y+k) & =1 \\\\ 7xy+kx & =1 \\\\ 7xy & =1-kx \\\\ y & =\\frac{1-kx}{7x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-kx}{7x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f55732d7-aca2-51a2-90ac-0f461a312d8c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f55732d7-aca2-51a2-90ac-0f461a312d8c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f55732d7-aca2-51a2-90ac-0f461a312d8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73fcfb27-eaff-5647-944c-46439323073f" "answer-1ac1e3c6-b482-5ff8-b9a9-e773f457d7b9" "answer-dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" "answer-5e2861d3-1422-5dd0-b377-19f88162a86e" "answer-76531f62-9097-54a3-ab2b-ca46f34bbee0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73fcfb27-eaff-5647-944c-46439323073f" :answer/id #uuid "73fcfb27-eaff-5647-944c-46439323073f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ac1e3c6-b482-5ff8-b9a9-e773f457d7b9" :answer/id #uuid "1ac1e3c6-b482-5ff8-b9a9-e773f457d7b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" :answer/id #uuid "dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e2861d3-1422-5dd0-b377-19f88162a86e" :answer/id #uuid "5e2861d3-1422-5dd0-b377-19f88162a86e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76531f62-9097-54a3-ab2b-ca46f34bbee0" :answer/id #uuid "76531f62-9097-54a3-ab2b-ca46f34bbee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3bd71fc1-9e9b-5a64-b8c7-ee650f7e3c32" :question/id #uuid "3bd71fc1-9e9b-5a64-b8c7-ee650f7e3c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-148539" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3}{kx-2}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{5x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{kx-2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{ky-2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3}{ky-2} \\\\ x(ky-2) & =3 \\\\ kxy-2x & =3 \\\\ kxy & =3+2x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3+2x}{kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{kx}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81ce0f55-8715-56de-87b9-343c421ef84c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81ce0f55-8715-56de-87b9-343c421ef84c" :answer-field/id #uuid "81ce0f55-8715-56de-87b9-343c421ef84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1856ebd-05b3-5b96-80e5-a49aeba1092f" "answer-3c0abf8c-85fb-551c-9ea5-437c81c3f948" "answer-f3e23358-fa26-5ecc-beff-81359458ba1a" "answer-eae4f622-afce-53d0-bbc6-e7205a79fc4c" "answer-b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1856ebd-05b3-5b96-80e5-a49aeba1092f" :answer/id #uuid "b1856ebd-05b3-5b96-80e5-a49aeba1092f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c0abf8c-85fb-551c-9ea5-437c81c3f948" :answer/id #uuid "3c0abf8c-85fb-551c-9ea5-437c81c3f948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3e23358-fa26-5ecc-beff-81359458ba1a" :answer/id #uuid "f3e23358-fa26-5ecc-beff-81359458ba1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eae4f622-afce-53d0-bbc6-e7205a79fc4c" :answer/id #uuid "eae4f622-afce-53d0-bbc6-e7205a79fc4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b" :answer/id #uuid "b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-36115cd9-9382-506b-9404-8a68bbaccae0" :question/id #uuid "36115cd9-9382-506b-9404-8a68bbaccae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-148588" :question/problem "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1},\\,x\\ne -1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+4},\\,x\\ne -4.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3-ky}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3-ky}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =3-ky \\\\ xy+x & =3-ky \\\\ xy+ky & =3-x \\\\ y(x+k) & =3-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3-x}{x+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+k}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d49e749e-69c5-5c58-ab0b-3f74366a64e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d49e749e-69c5-5c58-ab0b-3f74366a64e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "d49e749e-69c5-5c58-ab0b-3f74366a64e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bdcd4de5-18ea-5e4c-9b72-a2b6952a3a96" "answer-8372edf8-2062-5f14-bc0d-326bb8851d42" "answer-b355850a-c9b6-5f69-9884-3502d004fb16" "answer-eb6b8691-1372-5998-8571-69302ac6ed6f" "answer-5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdcd4de5-18ea-5e4c-9b72-a2b6952a3a96" :answer/id #uuid "bdcd4de5-18ea-5e4c-9b72-a2b6952a3a96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8372edf8-2062-5f14-bc0d-326bb8851d42" :answer/id #uuid "8372edf8-2062-5f14-bc0d-326bb8851d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b355850a-c9b6-5f69-9884-3502d004fb16" :answer/id #uuid "b355850a-c9b6-5f69-9884-3502d004fb16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb6b8691-1372-5998-8571-69302ac6ed6f" :answer/id #uuid "eb6b8691-1372-5998-8571-69302ac6ed6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12" :answer/id #uuid "5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193826 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll learn how to compute inverses of reciprocal functions.\n\nAs an example, let's consider the function $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{7}{2x+4}.\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{7}{2x+4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{7}{2y+4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{7}{2y+4} \\\\ x(2y+4) & =7 \\\\ 2xy+4x & =7 \\\\ 2xy & =7-4x \\\\ y & =\\frac{7-4x}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{7 - 4x}{2x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192864 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059668 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8aef3688-a7db-5a18-95f7-9c000401998b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059434 :question/problem "The point $(a,b)$ lies on the curve $y=x^4.$ Which of the following points **must** lie on $y = (x-2)^4-6?$ \n\nI. $(a-2, b-6)$\n\nII. $(a+2,b+ 6)$\n\nIII. $(a+2, b-6)$\n\nIV. $(a-2,b+ 6)$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot $y = (x-2)^4-6,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- First, we take the graph $y=x^4.$\n\n- Then, we shift the graph horizontally by $2$ units to the right and get the graph of $y=(x-2)^4.$ After this transformation, the point $(a,b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(a+2,b).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we shift the result vertically by $6$ units down and obtain the graph of $y = (x-2)^4-6.$ After this transformation, the point $(a+2,b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(a+2,b-6).\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe are told that the point $(a, b)$ lies on the graph of $y = x^4$, which means:\n\n$$\nb=a^4\n$$\n\nNow, we want to find which point must lie on the graph of:\n\n$$\ny = (x-2)^4-6\n$$\n\nLet’s test what happens when we substitute $x = a + 2$ into this new equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(a+2-2)^{4}-6 \\\\  & ={a}^{4}-6 \\\\  & =b-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, when $x = a + 2$, we get $y = b - 6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059669 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-55975c7c-e140-5b83-8d6a-51f167ef8423"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8aef3688-a7db-5a18-95f7-9c000401998b" :question/id #uuid "8aef3688-a7db-5a18-95f7-9c000401998b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158537" :question/problem "The point $(a,b)$ lies on the curve $y={e}^{x}.$ Which of the following points **must** lie on $y={e}^{2x}-3?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot $y={e}^{2x}-3,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- First, we take the graph $y={e}^{x}.$\n\n- Then, we stretch the graph by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis and get the graph of  $y={e}^{2x}.$ After this transformation, the point $(a,b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(\\frac{a}{2},b).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we shift the result vertically by $3$ units down and obtain the graph of $y={e}^{2x}-3.$ After this transformation, the point $(\\frac{a}{2},b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(\\frac{a}{2},b-3).\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nSince the point $(a,b)$ lies on the graph of $y={e}^{x}$, we have that ${e}^{a}=b.$\n\nNow consider the graph of $y={e}^{2x}-3.$ Substituting $x=\\frac{a}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2\\cdot (a/2)}-3 \\\\  & ={e}^{a}-3 \\\\  & =b-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{a}{2},b-3)$ must lie on $y={e}^{2x}-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-913d1116-3eaa-556f-b9b4-ea8a98a7fac9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-913d1116-3eaa-556f-b9b4-ea8a98a7fac9" :answer-field/id #uuid "913d1116-3eaa-556f-b9b4-ea8a98a7fac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-00ca160e-cb63-581e-915a-c85ad7372034" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e2798c6-7b71-50ce-a869-45a58fada49f" "answer-9b1c6067-70b9-52ab-819a-3361ccb30529" "answer-00ca160e-cb63-581e-915a-c85ad7372034" "answer-9c534194-d200-5f07-a6b7-e379535c43d8" "answer-66800e86-33bf-5c7b-be8f-c2cc33cda489"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e2798c6-7b71-50ce-a869-45a58fada49f" :answer/id #uuid "3e2798c6-7b71-50ce-a869-45a58fada49f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2a,b-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b1c6067-70b9-52ab-819a-3361ccb30529" :answer/id #uuid "9b1c6067-70b9-52ab-819a-3361ccb30529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{a}{2},3b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ca160e-cb63-581e-915a-c85ad7372034" :answer/id #uuid "00ca160e-cb63-581e-915a-c85ad7372034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{a}{2},b-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c534194-d200-5f07-a6b7-e379535c43d8" :answer/id #uuid "9c534194-d200-5f07-a6b7-e379535c43d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(a-3,2b)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66800e86-33bf-5c7b-be8f-c2cc33cda489" :answer/id #uuid "66800e86-33bf-5c7b-be8f-c2cc33cda489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(a-3,\\frac{b}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233534 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f488749-aaf8-567a-ab71-f4c449b380c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f488749-aaf8-567a-ab71-f4c449b380c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f488749-aaf8-5