nsure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186109417 :answer-field/choices 17592186109418] [:db/retract 17592186109417 :answer-field/choices 17592186109419] [:db/retract 17592186109417 :answer-field/choices 17592186109420] [:db/retract 17592186109417 :answer-field/choices 17592186109421] [:db/retract 17592186109417 :answer-field/choices 17592186109422] {:db/id 17592186110770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9de433c9-b3da-5c7d-a414-05618ea3bae5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9de433c9-b3da-5c7d-a414-05618ea3bae5" :question/id #uuid "9de433c9-b3da-5c7d-a414-05618ea3bae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-26365" :question/problem "![](images/65/65e89fcd8ae54d3c269c064f7c9f55a81f3a4dd847c4195550c8c2bf4251982f.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠BOA$ is a straight angle, $\\overset{\\to }{OD}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{OE}$ are the bisectors of $∠AOC$ and $∠BOC$, respectively. If $m∠DOC=4x$ and $m∠COE=5x$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/77/77adc8fb9c00bd21579a8697f8b11c228e3864e657f2b991be4d09b4c6f5a96d.png)\n\nSince $\\overset{\\to }{OD}$ is the bisector of $∠AOC$, we have \n\n$$\nm∠AOD=m∠DOC=4x.\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{\\to }{OE}$ is the bisector of $∠BOC$, we have \n\n$$\nm∠EOB=m∠COE=5x.\n$$\n\nNow, by the angle addition postulate, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD+m∠DOC+m∠EOB+m∠COE & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x+4x+5x+5x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 18x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6259dee-47bb-5440-9bda-09df267863c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6259dee-47bb-5440-9bda-09df267863c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6259dee-47bb-5440-9bda-09df267863c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d776491-c1ab-5501-82d2-91e21a03ca6d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d776491-c1ab-5501-82d2-91e21a03ca6d" "answer-a58b1640-8c7c-556f-8206-addcb17809a4" "answer-d6a53a49-98a0-54d5-93a8-aa0a17c35392" "answer-c105109e-b039-5a38-a13d-3f87e2d4f160" "answer-6a5c6c0b-7e8a-5766-9d6d-58dc5b683669"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d776491-c1ab-5501-82d2-91e21a03ca6d" :answer/id #uuid "3d776491-c1ab-5501-82d2-91e21a03ca6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{10}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a58b1640-8c7c-556f-8206-addcb17809a4" :answer/id #uuid "a58b1640-8c7c-556f-8206-addcb17809a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{12}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6a53a49-98a0-54d5-93a8-aa0a17c35392" :answer/id #uuid "d6a53a49-98a0-54d5-93a8-aa0a17c35392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c105109e-b039-5a38-a13d-3f87e2d4f160" :answer/id #uuid "c105109e-b039-5a38-a13d-3f87e2d4f160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a5c6c0b-7e8a-5766-9d6d-58dc5b683669" :answer/id #uuid "6a5c6c0b-7e8a-5766-9d6d-58dc5b683669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{8}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110767 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-da69f84c-0e57-51e1-a173-b362df890bdd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111282 :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e112d00ddcb34c30a490d1a71e3e0b4a2c698707e3890666ac4e299c3ca37cd.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠BOA$ is a straight angle,  and $\\overset{\\to }{OD}$ is the bisector of $∠COA.$ If $m∠BOD={107}^{∘},$ find $m∠BOC.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/2d/2d75ac364d71d8dd6cf35cfe7f8966b603c3cbee0bc5adff5f7dadf7468bab4c.png)\n\nSince the angles $∠DOA$ and $∠BOD$ are supplementary, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠DOA & ={180}^{∘}-m∠BOD \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{107}^{∘} \\\\  & ={73}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe bisector of an angle divides the angle into two congruent angles. Therefore,\n\n$$\nm∠DOA=m∠COD={73}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, by the angle addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOC & =m∠BOD-m∠COD \\\\  & ={107}^{∘}-{73}^{∘} \\\\  & ={34}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109417 :answer-field/correct "answer-92508f56-9787-5b76-a9fe-11533bf721df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df095c91-6c8f-5d26-856c-40dc63831c93" "answer-92508f56-9787-5b76-a9fe-11533bf721df" "answer-58d5e5f5-dd58-5582-8b38-6a124bf6d737" "answer-ff189e12-57b2-5448-9e85-6d8ad358c87d" "answer-8fce95cb-be82-56d7-af85-f23763b2574a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df095c91-6c8f-5d26-856c-40dc63831c93" :answer/id #uuid "df095c91-6c8f-5d26-856c-40dc63831c93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{19.5}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92508f56-9787-5b76-a9fe-11533bf721df" :answer/id #uuid "92508f56-9787-5b76-a9fe-11533bf721df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{34}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58d5e5f5-dd58-5582-8b38-6a124bf6d737" :answer/id #uuid "58d5e5f5-dd58-5582-8b38-6a124bf6d737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{53.5}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff189e12-57b2-5448-9e85-6d8ad358c87d" :answer/id #uuid "ff189e12-57b2-5448-9e85-6d8ad358c87d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{56}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fce95cb-be82-56d7-af85-f23763b2574a" :answer/id #uuid "8fce95cb-be82-56d7-af85-f23763b2574a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{73}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-da69f84c-0e57-51e1-a173-b362df890bdd" :question/id #uuid "da69f84c-0e57-51e1-a173-b362df890bdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-117152" :question/problem "![](images/18/187b52aa0450e940bd644f9d1ae560a735c7e10e18157ecba910a6a817c11797.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠BOA$ is a straight angle,  and $\\overset{\\to }{OC}$ is the bisector of $∠BOD.$ If $m∠DOA={58}^{∘},$ find $m∠COA.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/9d/9d7c5789c579b9292beb17ad03ae6239083ffa70fe5ec581da33cd488e365344.png)\n\nSince the angles $∠BOD$ and $∠DOA$ are supplementary, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠DOA \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{58}^{∘} \\\\  & ={122}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe bisector of an angle divides the angle into two congruent angles. Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COD & =\\frac{m∠BOD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{122}^{∘}}{2} \\\\  & ={61}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by the angle addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COA & =m∠COD+m∠DOA \\\\  & ={61}^{∘}+{58}^{∘} \\\\  & ={119}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38c3c80e-f2de-5e28-b208-78246bebe168"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38c3c80e-f2de-5e28-b208-78246bebe168" :answer-field/id #uuid "38c3c80e-f2de-5e28-b208-78246bebe168" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6adf9c64-77a8-5ff5-bdf3-534f65b4650e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9911e812-959a-52fd-ae15-08a54c3a2ece" "answer-9155be22-cd39-56bb-bf04-cbe9e114a3b4" "answer-6adf9c64-77a8-5ff5-bdf3-534f65b4650e" "answer-a52a4974-7051-5d8f-a0eb-e62fe95403da" "answer-c8af1589-4ba3-59d6-8c49-d7530c09dc65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9911e812-959a-52fd-ae15-08a54c3a2ece" :answer/id #uuid "9911e812-959a-52fd-ae15-08a54c3a2ece" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{107}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9155be22-cd39-56bb-bf04-cbe9e114a3b4" :answer/id #uuid "9155be22-cd39-56bb-bf04-cbe9e114a3b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{113}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6adf9c64-77a8-5ff5-bdf3-534f65b4650e" :answer/id #uuid "6adf9c64-77a8-5ff5-bdf3-534f65b4650e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{119}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a52a4974-7051-5d8f-a0eb-e62fe954